---
description: Naming conventions for Monica Companion app covering file names, class names, variables, constants, methods, and test files. Enforces consistent snake_case files, PascalCase classes, camelCase variables, and proper private member prefixing to ensure readable maintainable code across the entire Flutter project.
globs: ["**/*.dart", "**/*.yaml", "**/*.md"]
alwaysApply: true
---

## File Naming Conventions

- Use snake_case for files
- Include descriptive functionality names
- Add _test suffix for tests
- Match file to primary class
- Keep names concise but clear

```
// Good - snake_case files
app_config.dart              # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
feature_state.dart           # @lib/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart
validators_test.dart         # @test/core/utils/validators_test.dart
environment.dart             # @lib/core/config/environment.dart

// Bad - other cases
AppConfig.dart
featureState.dart
ValidatorsTest.dart
```

## Class and Type Naming

- Use PascalCase for classes
- Use PascalCase for enums
- Include descriptive purpose suffixes
- Avoid abbreviations unless common
- Make purpose immediately clear

```dart
// Good - PascalCase classes
class MonicaApp extends StatelessWidget {}    # @lib/main.dart
class WelcomeScreen extends StatelessWidget {} # @lib/main.dart
class AppConfig {}                            # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
class FeatureState extends Equatable {}       # @lib/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart
class LoadingState extends FeatureState {}
class ErrorState extends FeatureState {}

// Bad - other cases
class monicaApp {}
class welcome_screen {}
class appconfig {}
```

## Variable and Method Naming

- Use camelCase for variables
- Use camelCase for methods
- Make purpose descriptive and clear
- Avoid single letter names
- Include type context when helpful

```dart
// Good - camelCase variables and methods
final String appName = 'Monica Companion';           # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
static Duration get defaultTimeout => Duration();    # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
final int maxRetryAttempts = 3;                     # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
static String get packageName => packageNameBase;   # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart

// Bad - other cases
final String app_name;
final String AppName;
static Duration get default_timeout;
```

## Constant Naming Conventions

- Use camelCase for class constants
- Use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for globals
- Include descriptive context clearly
- Group related constants together
- Make purpose immediately obvious

```dart
// Good - constant naming
static const String version = '1.0.0';              # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
static const int maxRetryAttempts = 3;               # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
static const Duration defaultSyncInterval = Duration(hours: 4); # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
static const String packageNameBase = 'fr.m0hdaCorp.monica_companion'; # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart

// For widget-specific constants
static const Color _monicaBrandColor = Color(0xFF6366F1);  # @lib/main.dart
static const double _mainPadding = 24;                     # @lib/main.dart
static const double _sectionSpacing = 40;                  # @lib/main.dart
```

## Private Member Naming

- Prefix with underscore always
- Use camelCase after underscore
- Apply to private fields
- Apply to private methods
- Keep scope minimal and clear

```dart
// Good - private member naming
static const Color _monicaBrandColor = Color(0xFF6366F1);  # @lib/main.dart
static const double _mainPadding = 24;                     # @lib/main.dart
static const double _sectionSpacing = 40;                  # @lib/main.dart

class AppConfig {
  AppConfig._();  // Private constructor
}
```

## Test File Naming

- Add _test suffix always
- Mirror source file structure
- Use same base name
- Include descriptive test purpose
- Group tests by functionality

```
