## Package and Import Naming

- Use snake_case package names
- Include organization prefix consistently
- Keep import aliases short
- Use meaningful package names
- Follow Dart conventions exactly

```dart
// Good - package naming
name: monica_companion                    # @pubspec.yaml
package:monica_companion/core/config/     # Import structure

// Import examples
import 'package:monica_companion/core/config/app_config.dart';           # @lib/main.dart
import 'package:monica_companion/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart';
```

## Boolean and State Naming

- Use descriptive boolean prefixes
- Start with is/has/can/should
- Make state purpose clear
- Avoid negative boolean names
- Include context when needed

```dart
// Good - boolean naming
static bool get isDebug => EnvironmentConfig.isDevelopment;  # @lib/core/config/app_config.dart
bool get isValidEmail => Validators.isValidEmail(email);
bool get hasData => data != null;
bool get canSubmit => isValid && isNotEmpty;
```